  "visual": {
    "visualType": "textbox",
    "objects": {
      "general": [
        {
          "properties": {
            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Tips",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "20pt",
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "color": "#091612"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": " ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "6pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "•  Waterfall mode = Comparison (General card): every measure in the Value bucket becomes a pillar, baseline first (Actual M-1 → Actual), and the bridges decompose the gap category by category.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#091612"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": " ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "6pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "•  The rail above each gap reads the measure in the Variance bucket ([Δ M-1 %]), computed on the engine’s bar-grain subtotal, so ratios stay exact.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#091612"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": " ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "6pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "•  Y axis → Floor offset (75 % here) starts the axis near the pillar bases so the deltas become readable; the striped broken-axis marker flags the cut honestly.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#091612"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": " ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "6pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "•  Bridge fills are a conditional fx on [Δ M-1] (Bridges → Bridge colour): red when the category lost vs the baseline, green when it gained.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#091612"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": " ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "6pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "•  Each measure-pillar has its own fill and label styling (Pillars card, per-measure).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#091612"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": " ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "6pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "•  Three or more measures work too: every consecutive pair of pillars gets its own bridges and rail.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#091612"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": " ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "6pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "•  Comparison needs a Category field: without one, the visual falls back to Cumulative.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#091612"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": " ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "6pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
